<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32185" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">octāvus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		octo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the eighth</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">octava pars,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 15, 26, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 2, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marmor,</span>”
				<i>the eighth mile-stone</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					9, 65, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">octāva</span></b> , ae, f.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> (Sc. hora.) <i>The eighth hour of the day</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 4, 8,
				5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 1, 49</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> (Sc. pars.) <i>The
				eighth part</i>, as a tax, <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 4,
				65, 7</span></i>; Cod. Th. 4, 12, 6; <i><span class="en">Ulp.
				Fragm. 6, 12</span></i> (cf. octavarius).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">octāvum</span></b> , <i>for the eighth
			time</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 6, 36, 7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
